WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.625
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:35.166
<b>Krishna explained that Arjuna, and we,</b>

3
00:00:35.166 --> 00:00:41.041
<b>should perform our duties free from </b>
<b>expectation, ego, and lethargy,</b>

4
00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:48.666
<b>while offering these actions at</b>
<b>Krishna's feet with devotion.</b>

5
00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:51.916
<b>This verse now describes</b>

6
00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:58.208
<b>the outcome of dedicating our actions </b>
<b>to Krishna with devotion.</b>

7
00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:02.333
<b>The consequences of not doing so</b>

8
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:06.708
<b>will be explained in the next verse, </b>
<b>the thirty-second one.</b>

9
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.916
<b>In this verse, Krishna states</b>

10
00:01:13.916 --> 00:01:19.958
<b>that those who follow my teachings </b>
<b>with complete faith and without envy</b>

11
00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:23.208
<b>become free from the bondage of karma.</b>

12
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:29.416
<b>Freedom from karmic bondage means </b>
<b>liberation from the chains of sin and virtue.</b>

13
00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:34.791
<b>This liberation from karmic bondage was also </b>
<b>mentioned in the ninth verse of the third chapter,</b>

14
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:38.250
<b>where it was said that if actions </b>
<b>are performed as sacrifice</b>

15
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.916
<b>and offered to Lord Vishnu, one can be</b>
<b>freed from sin and virtue.</b>

16
00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:46.333
<b>The same principle applies here.</b>

17
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:50.291
<b>The essence is that by treating work </b>
<b>as devotion and sacrifice,</b>

18
00:01:50.291 --> 00:01:54.375
<b>and offering it to the Divine, </b>
<b>one finds the path to liberation.</b>

19
00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:57.250
<b>There's another important point </b>
<b>to understand in this verse –</b>

20
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.625
<b>Krishna says</b>

21
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:05.125
<b>those who follow my teachings with</b>
<b>faith will be freed from karmic bondage.</b>

22
00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.333
<b>You too have been a student,</b>

23
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:11.833
<b>and know that receiving </b>
<b>education, understanding its lessons,</b>

24
00:02:11.833 --> 00:02:17.541
<b>incorporating them into your life, and finally</b>
<b>following those teachings completely –</b>

25
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:21.416
<b>this is a process that takes time.</b>

26
00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:23.416
<b>This is what we must understand.</b>

27
00:02:23.416 --> 00:02:26.666
<b>We must give it time, maintain patience.</b>

28
00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>Often, people study Vedic knowledge</b>

29
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.708
<b>and become discouraged when </b>
<b>they can't follow it perfectly.</b>

30
00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:40.083
<b>They think that if they cannot follow it, </b>
<b>either the teaching must be wrong</b>

31
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:42.916
<b>or its practice impossible.</b>

32
00:02:42.916 --> 00:02:46.041
<b>This impatience and despair isn't right.</b>

33
00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:51.166
<b>It's because of this that many people halt</b>
<b>their spiritual progress midway.</b>

34
00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:52.291
<b>Faith,</b>

35
00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:53.125
<b>time,</b>

36
00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:54.208
<b>and patience –</b>

37
00:02:54.208 --> 00:02:59.083
<b>these three are essential for </b>
<b>completely following any teaching,</b>

38
00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:02.708
<b>no matter how simple it may seem.</b>

39
00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:08.166
<b>And here we're talking about freedom </b>
<b>from karmic bondage, from sin and virtue.</b>

40
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:12.416
<b>We're discussing the very purpose </b>
<b>of our entire life on Earth.</b>

41
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:17.291
<b>This Gita has guided humanity </b>
<b>for thousands of years.</b>

42
00:03:17.291 --> 00:03:18.916
<b>It will guide you too.</b>

43
00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:20.208
<b>Give it time,</b>

44
00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:22.500
<b>maintain faith and patience.</b>

45
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.958
<b>Keep making continuous efforts,</b>

46
00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:26.750
<b>don't abandon them."</b>

47
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.375
<b>This verse speaks about following teachings.</b>

48
00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:36.750
<b>Think</b>

49
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.166
<b>back to when you learned something new,</b>

50
00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:44.166
<b>especially something </b>
<b>that could transform your life.</b>

51
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:45.625
<b>For instance,</b>

52
00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:52.208
<b>you started a new exercise or </b>
<b>yoga routine for health improvement,</b>

53
00:03:52.208 --> 00:03:56.458
<b>began a new course in some subject,</b>

54
00:03:56.458 --> 00:04:02.458
<b>or initiated changes for spiritual growth.</b>

55
00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:05.416
<b>The greater the intended change,</b>

56
00:04:05.416 --> 00:04:08.291
<b>the more complex the teaching appears,</b>

57
00:04:08.291 --> 00:04:13.333
<b>and the more challenging </b>
<b>the process of change seems.</b>

58
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:17.083
<b>This is especially true in the beginning days.</b>

59
00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.458
<b>Your mind will resist exercise,</b>

60
00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:20.916
<b>your body will protest,</b>

61
00:04:20.916 --> 00:04:23.541
<b>tasty foods will tempt you,</b>

62
00:04:23.541 --> 00:04:28.208
<b>You'll feel discouraged,</b>

63
00:04:28.208 --> 00:04:36.291
<b>and sometimes think that</b>
<b>things were better as they were.</b>

64
00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:38.875
<b>Has this happened to you?</b>

65
00:04:38.875 --> 00:04:40.250
<b>Hasn't it?</b>

66
00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.041
<b>But the Gita teaches this...</b>

67
00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:44.083
<b>faith,</b>

68
00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.166
<b>time,</b>

69
00:04:45.166 --> 00:04:48.375
<b>and patience.</b>

70
00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:50.208
<b>Instead of getting discouraged,</b>

71
00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:53.875
<b>you must show faith in the process of change,</b>

72
00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:56.041
<b>give it time,</b>

73
00:04:56.041 --> 00:04:58.583
<b>maintain patience,</b>

74
00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:03.208
<b>without being disturbed </b>
<b>by when results will come.</b>

75
00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:07.250
<b>It's just like planting a seed –</b>

76
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:11.333
<b>you prepare the soil, provide water and sunlight,</b>

77
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:12.416
<b>but</b>

78
00:05:12.416 --> 00:05:17.833
<b>you cannot force the seed to </b>
<b>sprout before its time.</b>

79
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:19.916
<b>The seed is beneath the earth,</b>

80
00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:23.500
<b>no change will be visible for many days,</b>

81
00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.750
<b>it will seem like all efforts are futile,</b>

82
00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.666
<b>and then one day,</b>

83
00:05:28.666 --> 00:05:31.541
<b>when the time is right and the seed sprouts,</b>

84
00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:35.916
<b>a new energy of faith will awaken within you.</b>

85
00:05:35.916 --> 00:05:38.916
<b>Personal transformation is just like this.</b>

86
00:05:38.916 --> 00:05:42.833
<b>When you begin any teaching or new routine,</b>

87
00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:49.125
<b>the changes happening inside your </b>
<b>body and mind aren't visible for some time.</b>

88
00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>But if you consistently provide the </b>
<b>sunlight of faith and the water of patience,</b>

89
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:59.375
<b>the seed of change you've planted </b>
<b>in your mind and body</b>

90
00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:01.250
<b>will surely sprout.</b>

91
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:06.125
<b>Spiritual and personal growth is a long path;</b>

92
00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:12.041
<b>thinking repeatedly about the </b>
<b>destination won't bring it any closer.</b>

93
00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:18.041
<b>It comes closer only by continuing </b>
<b>to walk the right path.</b>

94
00:06:18.041 --> 00:06:19.750
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

95
00:06:23.875 --> 00:06:27.416
<b>Many moments will come in life</b>

96
00:06:27.416 --> 00:06:34.333
<b>when you'll feel your loved ones aren't </b>
<b>progressing according to your expectations.</b>

97
00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:40.333
<b>Perhaps you might even feel </b>
<b>they don't want to progress.</b>

98
00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:44.375
<b>Such differences and doubts </b>
<b>can certainly arise in the mind.</b>

99
00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:46.000
<b>For example,</b>

100
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.291
<b>you might start wondering</b>

101
00:06:48.291 --> 00:06:52.291
<b>why your child isn't following your advice,</b>

102
00:06:52.291 --> 00:06:56.750
<b>thinking they would progress </b>
<b>better if they listened to you,</b>

103
00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.208
<b>but they keep getting distracted by other things.</b>

104
00:07:01.208 --> 00:07:04.708
<b>This must have happened with you.</b>

105
00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:06.958
<b>Hasn't it?</b>

106
00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:13.041
<b>In such moments, never give space to</b>
<b>disappointment and impatience in your mind.</b>

107
00:07:13.041 --> 00:07:17.750
<b>Look at this situation from a </b>
<b>student and teacher's perspective.</b>

108
00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:22.041
<b>Consider yourself as a student.</b>

109
00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:24.708
<b>What kind of teacher would be better?</b>

110
00:07:24.708 --> 00:07:30.333
<b>One who quickly loses patience and scolds?</b>

111
00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:33.291
<b>Or a teacher who understands you,</b>

112
00:07:33.291 --> 00:07:39.708
<b>never tries to suggest there's </b>
<b>something wrong with you,</b>

113
00:07:39.708 --> 00:07:47.333
<b>always encourages you, and explains with </b>
<b>affection and, above all, patience?</b>

114
00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.708
<b>You too have been a child, haven't you?</b>

115
00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:56.666
<b>Your parents wanted you to </b>
<b>learn everything quickly,</b>

116
00:07:56.666 --> 00:07:59.125
<b>but contrary to their expectations,</b>

117
00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:03.833
<b>you too took your time learning life's lessons.</b>

118
00:08:03.833 --> 00:08:05.041
<b>Didn’t you?</b>

119
00:08:05.041 --> 00:08:09.166
<b>But everything turned out fine in the end, didn't it?</b>

120
00:08:09.166 --> 00:08:10.458
<b>Then</b>

121
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:14.375
<b>why such impatience about your children?</b>

122
00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:17.541
<b>Why such disappointment?</b>

123
00:08:17.541 --> 00:08:22.375
<b>Can you force a seed to sprout quickly?</b>

124
00:08:22.375 --> 00:08:23.791
<b>No.</b>

125
00:08:23.791 --> 00:08:30.916
<b>Who is harmed by being disturbed by </b>
<b>this slow pace of the seed's sprouting?</b>

126
00:08:30.916 --> 00:08:34.625
<b>Both you and the seed.</b>

127
00:08:34.625 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>You'll be disturbed,</b>

128
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:37.791
<b>you'll feel discouraged...</b>

129
00:08:37.791 --> 00:08:42.041
<b>and then in this discouragement, </b>
<b>you might lose patience,</b>

130
00:08:42.041 --> 00:08:45.125
<b>stop giving water and sunlight,</b>

131
00:08:45.125 --> 00:08:49.000
<b>stop taking care out of frustration.</b>

132
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.041
<b>Both suffer in this.</b>

133
00:08:52.041 --> 00:08:53.958
<b>What's right?</b>

134
00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:55.416
<b>Maintaining patience,</b>

135
00:08:55.416 --> 00:08:59.000
<b>and doing whatever you can from your end.</b>

136
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:04.166
<b>Giving water on time, adding fertilizer, </b>
<b>protecting from harsh sun when needed.</b>

137
00:09:04.166 --> 00:09:06.958
<b>Now think,</b>

138
00:09:06.958 --> 00:09:12.916
<b>your child is also like such a seed.</b>

139
00:09:12.916 --> 00:09:15.583
<b>Keep providing the water of guidance,</b>

140
00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:20.416
<b>be their shade when needed in </b>
<b>the harsh sun of challenges,</b>

141
00:09:20.416 --> 00:09:25.208
<b>keep adding the fertilizer of knowledge </b>
<b>in the right measure at the right time.</b>

142
00:09:25.208 --> 00:09:30.125
<b>The seed will not only sprout but </b>
<b>will grow and flourish healthily.</b>

143
00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:37.083
<b>This same principle can be applied to </b>
<b>other relationships with loved ones.</b>

144
00:09:37.083 --> 00:09:38.625
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

145
00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:48.458
<b>If your workplace is one where </b>
<b>there's pressure to achieve targets,</b>

146
00:09:48.458 --> 00:09:53.833
<b>pressure to complete every task before deadlines,</b>

147
00:09:53.833 --> 00:09:55.500
<b>then in such an environment,</b>

148
00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.625
<b>if work doesn't go according to plan,</b>

149
00:09:58.625 --> 00:10:01.333
<b>or if workload increases,</b>

150
00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:04.708
<b>sometimes patience runs out,</b>

151
00:10:04.708 --> 00:10:09.041
<b>sometimes anger is felt, </b>
<b>frustration is experienced.</b>

152
00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:11.333
<b>But the truth is,</b>

153
00:10:11.333 --> 00:10:15.166
<b>losing patience, feeling anger and frustration</b>

154
00:10:15.166 --> 00:10:19.750
<b>never improve situations -</b>
<b>they can certainly make them worse.</b>

155
00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:25.791
<b>Learning patience and faith in pressured or </b>
<b>stressful environments is not only helpful</b>

156
00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:29.333
<b>but extremely important.</b>

157
00:10:29.333 --> 00:10:30.958
<b>For example,</b>

158
00:10:30.958 --> 00:10:34.083
<b>if you're in a leadership position,</b>

159
00:10:34.083 --> 00:10:40.041
<b>and there's an unexpected delay in a project,</b>

160
00:10:40.041 --> 00:10:43.125
<b>or a colleague makes a mistake,</b>

161
00:10:43.125 --> 00:10:50.125
<b>public criticism and anger are the easiest paths.</b>

162
00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:54.875
<b>But by doing this, we're only looking </b>
<b>for someone to blame,</b>

163
00:10:54.875 --> 00:10:57.083
<b>not solving the problem.</b>

164
00:10:57.083 --> 00:10:59.375
<b>If you're in a leadership position,</b>

165
00:10:59.375 --> 00:11:05.791
<b>first understand that such </b>
<b>situations will arise many times.</b>

166
00:11:05.791 --> 00:11:08.333
<b>If everything went according to schedule,</b>

167
00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:12.000
<b>if all colleagues worked at peak capacity,</b>

168
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.666
<b>if everything was perfect,</b>

169
00:11:14.666 --> 00:11:18.166
<b>then where would be the need for leadership?</b>

170
00:11:18.166 --> 00:11:21.916
<b>Leadership is needed because</b>

171
00:11:21.916 --> 00:11:26.625
<b>someone must be there who </b>
<b>elevates their colleagues' work level,</b>

172
00:11:26.625 --> 00:11:29.166
<b>who finds solutions to problems,</b>

173
00:11:29.166 --> 00:11:34.916
<b>who learns from problems </b>
<b>so they can be avoided in the future.</b>

174
00:11:34.916 --> 00:11:36.125
<b>So then,</b>

175
00:11:36.125 --> 00:11:42.666
<b>getting caught up in negative emotions like </b>
<b>criticism and anger is futile, isn't it?</b>

176
00:11:42.666 --> 00:11:44.333
<b>However,</b>

177
00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:47.416
<b>if you patiently understand</b>

178
00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:49.500
<b>what went wrong, </b>

179
00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:54.416
<b>suggest ways to correct your colleague's mistake,</b>

180
00:11:54.416 --> 00:11:59.000
<b>and show faith in them for the future,</b>

181
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.958
<b>not only will working relationships improve,</b>

182
00:12:01.958 --> 00:12:02.833
<b>but</b>

183
00:12:02.833 --> 00:12:06.291
<b>the entire environment will become positive.</b>

184
00:12:06.291 --> 00:12:09.583
<b>If someone criticizes you publicly?</b>

185
00:12:09.583 --> 00:12:12.750
<b>lose patience towards you?</b>

186
00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:18.166
<b>Do you think this will increase </b>
<b>your work efficiency?</b>

187
00:12:18.166 --> 00:12:19.416
<b>No, right?</b>

188
00:12:19.416 --> 00:12:20.916
<b>Then,</b>

189
00:12:20.916 --> 00:12:27.291
<b>how can such behavior be effective </b>
<b>with colleagues working under you?</b>

190
00:12:27.291 --> 00:12:31.916
<b>Everyone shines in the light of patience and faith.</b>

191
00:12:31.916 --> 00:12:35.125
<b>Practice these at your workplace.</b>

192
00:12:35.125 --> 00:12:40.583
<b>These two are the main ingredients </b>
<b>in the recipe of leadership.</b>

193
00:12:40.583 --> 00:12:42.000
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

